## Step 2: Assess Validation Status

**17-0add-22deg-200s-N2-1450s**: This condition has been run many times (runs 1–9 in the recent campaign). However, pore fraction is only reported for run1. The subsequent runs (2–9) all lack pore fraction measurements. Multiple measurements of one specimen ≠ synthesis reproducibility, but these appear to be independent synthesis runs. The modulus varies widely across runs (161–310 bar), suggesting high synthesis variability. Pore fraction is unknown for runs 2–9.

**16p5-0add-19deg-175s-N2-1450s**: Run1 has modulus=437.9 (very high, CV=0.093, large SD=102 bar) and pore fraction=0.394 (low). Run2 has modulus=196.9 (much lower) and pore fraction=unknown. These two runs are highly inconsistent — the modulus dropped dramatically. This candidate is NOT confirmed.

**17-0add-5deg-90s-N2-1800s_run2**: Modulus=356.6, Pore Fraction=0.569. Only one synthesis run at these exact parameters (run3 used speed=20 instead of 18). Not independently validated.

## Step 3: Pareto Analysis

Looking at the non-dominated set (both objectives measured, quality acceptable):

- **17-0add-22deg-200s-N2-1450s run1**: Modulus=261.9, PF=0.618 — high PF, moderate modulus, good quality
- **17-0add-5deg-90s-N2-1800s_run2**: Modulus=356.6, PF=0.569 — higher modulus, slightly lower PF, wrinkle defect, 1 discarded fit
- **17-0add-15deg-30s-N2-1200s**: Modulus=355.3, PF=0.459 — high modulus, lower PF
- **16p5-0add-19deg-175s-N2-1450s**: Modulus=437.9, PF=0.394 — highest modulus seen, but very low PF and not reproduced

The 17-0add-22deg-200s-N2-1450s condition (run1) is a strong Pareto candidate for high pore fraction. However, the subsequent runs show highly variable modulus (161–310 bar) with pore fraction unknown. The original run1 pore fraction (0.618) has not been independently confirmed.

## Step 4: Decision

The 17-0add-22deg-200s-N2-1450s condition (polymer_wt=17.0, bath_temp=22, pullcast_speed=19, nitrogen=True, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=200, nips_bath_wait_time=1450, mixing_temp=25) is a Pareto-front candidate with the highest confirmed pore fraction (0.618) among good-quality membranes, combined with reasonable modulus (261.9 bar). However:

- Pore fraction has only been measured once (run1)
- Subsequent runs show modulus variability (161–310 bar range across 9 runs)
- The condition needs pore fraction confirmed on an independent synthesis

This is a clear validation priority: the pore fraction of 0.618 is the best confirmed value in the dataset for a good-quality membrane, but it rests on a single measurement. The modulus variability across runs is concerning and needs characterization with pore fraction co-measured.

